<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harthacnut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1018–1042</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Hardicanute</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harthacnut was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> from 1035 and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from 1040 to 1042, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cnut-the-great">Cnut the Great</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emma-of-normandy">Emma of Normandy</a>. Kept in Denmark by the threat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-the-good">Magnus the Good</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, he lost England for a time to his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harold-harefoot">Harold Harefoot</a> but took the throne after Harold's death. His heavy taxes made him unpopular, and his sudden death at a wedding feast in 1042 brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor">Edward the Confessor</a> to the English throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harthacnut.jpg" alt="Harthacnut" width="320" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harthacnut_-_MS_Royal_14_B_VI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
